 I ask myself for several days why user profile fields were still editable whereas my policy settings in our custom auth plugin was well recorded. I found the answer debugging in the database: 
```text
select *


from mdl_auth_custom


order by id desc ;
```
 Our auth plugin (in house dev) stores its settings under `auth_custom` whereas the function `print_auth_lock_options` (moodle CORE) stores settings under `auth/custom`. Thus, when `$authplugin = get_auth_plugin($user->auth);` is called it only retrieves settings under `auth_custom`. That's why fields lock policy was not applied (since stored under `auth/custom`). I fixed that merging the 2 objects settings in our auth constructor: 
```text
    /**


     * Constructor.


     * merge the settings under `auth_custom` with `auth/custom` to retrieve settings that manage user profile lock policy.


     * @see : 
https://moodle.org/mod/forum/discuss.php?d=377951


     */


    function auth_plugin_custom()


    {


        $this->authtype = 'custom';


        $this->config = get_config('auth_custom');


        foreach (get_config('auth/custom') as $property => $value) {


            $this->config->$property = $value;


        }


    }
```
 This is now working fine. We can manage user fields that we want to lock in our custom auth plugin. A refactoring will be needed to make our plugin settings saved its settings under `auth/custom`.

